---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "How to Estimate Property Taxes for a Mortgage Payment";
const description =
  "Estimate property taxes for a mortgage payment using local rates and recent bills so your inputs are realistic. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-08";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/how-to-estimate-property-taxes" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Property taxes</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>How to estimate property taxes</h1>
    <p>
      Property taxes can materially change your monthly housing payment. Use local tax rates and recent bills to avoid
      underestimating your mortgage payment.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/what-is-piti">What is PITI?</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where to get tax numbers</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>County or city tax assessor websites (current millage or tax rate).</li>
      <li>Recent tax bills for similar homes in the same area.</li>
      <li>Your real estate agent or lender estimate (verify with public data).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Estimate approach (quick)</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Find the local tax rate or recent tax bill.</li>
      <li>Multiply the tax rate by the assessed value (or purchase price if applicable).</li>
      <li>Divide the annual tax by 12 to get the monthly amount.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Property tax estimate example</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If the tax rate is 1.1% and the assessed value is $400,000, annual tax is about $4,400 and the monthly estimate is about $367.
      Use this monthly number in your mortgage payment calculator inputs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Assessment vs purchase price</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Some areas reassess taxes after a sale. If you are buying, use the expected post-sale assessed value instead of the
      current owner's bill to avoid underestimating your taxes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Escrow changes after closing</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Taxes and insurance can change after closing, which can raise the escrow portion of your payment. Budget a cushion so
      the first escrow adjustment does not surprise you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using the seller's current tax bill without accounting for reassessment.</li>
      <li>Leaving out special assessments or local fees that show on tax bills.</li>
      <li>Assuming taxes are flat when local rates can change annually.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/how-mortgage-payments-are-calculated">How mortgage payments are calculated</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/principal-and-interest-vs-escrow">Principal and interest vs escrow</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do property taxes show up in my mortgage payment?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Usually yes if your lender escrows taxes. If you pay taxes separately, exclude them from the escrow portion and budget
      for the annual bill.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can my tax estimate be wrong after I buy?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. Reassessments and tax rate changes can increase the bill. Use a conservative estimate and re-check after closing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Run the mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/how-to-estimate-homeowners-insurance">Estimate homeowners insurance</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

